Adaptive macOS icon asset maintenance. The Icon Composer source keeps square unmasked layers, with system-dark and tintable Mono specializations. The legacy fallback is rendered from the Default appearance into all standard macOS iconset slots and compiled with /usr/bin/iconutil so pre-Tahoe systems receive rounded transparent corners at the full resolution set. The standard-library verifier parses the ICNS structure and embedded PNGs, checks required sizes, RGBA format, and transparent corners. CI failure root cause was fork pull requests lacking PRIVATE_REPOS_TOKEN during private submodule checkout; the corrected branch is being moved to the upstream repository so existing CI can run without weakening checkout security.
